+- **Evidence self-check before delivery**: `kc evidence check` re-runs each `evidence.json` command with the delivery gate's own parser, timeout and `stdout_assertions` judgment, lists every failure in one pass, and prints the expected substring plus the closest actual output line. An evidence block that declares `stdout_assertions` must pass this first. `--timeout` may only shorten the gate limit (default 300s; larger values exit `2`); exit codes are `0` all passed / `1` failures / `2` usage error, and `--json` emits `{passed, summary, items, manifest_errors}` on stdout. Passing the self-check does not replace the gate — environment differences can still fail it.
